{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrierEquiv","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrierEquiv","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCarrierEquiv","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BalancedGenerators","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Coxeter.Matrix"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.skeinCoxeterEquiv_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.skeinCoxeterEquiv_σ","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L307-L315","doc":"The composite sends the skein generator `σ_i` to `q⁻¹ • T_i` — the §7a rescaling,\nnow landing in the Coxeter presentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.skeinBalancedEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.skeinBalancedEquiv","kind":"def","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L292-L305","doc":"**The target is *literally* `Balanced.BalancedHecke`**, not merely isomorphic to it.\n\n`BalancedHecke M q` is by definition `HeckeAlgebra R (q * q) M`, so taking `Q = q * q`\ndirectly in `carrierEquiv` — rather than composing through `skeinIwahoriEquiv`, which\nfixes `q ^ 2` — lands on that object on the nose, with no transport along `pow_two`.\n\nThis is what makes the headline claim checkable rather than asserted: the algebra on the\nleft carries the proved-unique Ocneanu trace, and the algebra on the right is the one\n`IwahoriHecke/BalancedGenerators.lean` builds its §7a generators `σ_i = qi · T_i` on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.skeinCoxeterEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.skeinCoxeterEquiv","kind":"def","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L287-L290","doc":"**`H^skein_n(q) ≃ₐ HeckeAlgebra K q² (Aₙ n)`** over a field, for `q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.coxeterCarrierEquiv_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.coxeterCarrierEquiv_σ","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L277-L279","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.coxeterCarrierEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.coxeterCarrierEquiv","kind":"def","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L259-L275","doc":"**The two presentations are the same algebra.**\n\nBoth composites are the identity on generators, so `hom_ext` on each side finishes. No\nhypothesis on `Q` is needed: unlike the *normalisation* change of\n`QOU.SchurWeyl.carrierEquiv`, this is a change of how the relations are *written*, and no\nscalar is inverted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.fromCoxeter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.fromCoxeter","kind":"def","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L250-L256","doc":"**Coxeter presentation → `Fin n` presentation**, `T_i ↦ σ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.toCoxeter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.toCoxeter","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L237-L247","doc":"**`Fin n` presentation → Coxeter presentation**, `σ_i ↦ T_i`.\n\nThe parameter does not move and the generators map across on the nose; all that is\nchecked is that the `T_i` satisfy the two explicit clauses, which they do by\n`braid_of_altProd` / `comm_of_altProd` applied to `T_braid`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.quadratic_smul_iff_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.quadratic_smul_iff_factored","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L213-L232","doc":"The two spellings of the Hecke quadratic relation agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.comm_of_altProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.comm_of_altProd","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L197-L206","doc":"**The `altProd` clause implies far commutation.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.braid_of_altProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.braid_of_altProd","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L182-L195","doc":"**The `altProd` clause implies adjacent braiding.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.altProd_of_explicit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.altProd_of_explicit","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L144-L180","doc":"**The explicit clauses imply the `altProd` clause.**\n\nFive cases on `(i : ℕ)` against `(j : ℕ)`: equal (diagonal, entry `1`, `altProd _ _ 1 = a`\non both sides), `i + 1 = j` and `j + 1 = i` (the two orientations of the braid, entry `3`),\nand `j + 2 ≤ i` and `i + 2 ≤ j` (the two orientations of far commutation, entry `2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.AMat_far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.AMat_far","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L111-L118","doc":"Distinct non-adjacent indices commute: the entry is `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.AMat_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.AMat_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L102-L109","doc":"Adjacent indices braid: the entry is `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.AMat_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.AMat_diag","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L98-L100","doc":"On the diagonal the entry is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.AMat_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.AMat_symm","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L94-L96","doc":"The matrix is symmetric — this is `CoxeterMatrix`'s own field, not a fresh proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.AMat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.CoxeterCarrier.AMat","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/CoxeterCarrierEquiv.lean#L91-L92","doc":"The type-`Aₙ` Coxeter matrix on `Fin n`, as the bare function `HeckeAlgebra` wants. ","signatureChunk":0}]}